# What the image build needs is the Go module and the three asset trees
# go:embed reaches for: templates, web/static and web/app/dist. None of those
# are listed here, and nothing below may ever grow a pattern that swallows
# them -- an excluded asset tree fails at embed time with a message about a
# missing directory rather than at run time, but it is still an hour lost.

.git
.github
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
.goreleaser.yaml
Makefile

# The host's own build output. Copying it in would drop a darwin binary into a
# linux image, and the COPY would silently win over the one this build just
# produced.
/dist
/playground
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Installed inside the builder, never carried in from the host: node_modules is
# large, platform-specific, and unused by a build that only compiles Go.
web/app/node_modules
examples/playwright-ts/node_modules

# Reference suites, prose and the planning document. None of them is embedded,
# so all any of them can do here is invalidate the build cache.
examples
docs
*.md

# Editors and OS droppings.
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
.playwright-mcp
